25. TESTING AND ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

Create automated tests where practical, including:

- Unit tests.
- Repository tests.
- API tests.
- Authentication and authorization tests.
- Database migration tests.
- Integration contract tests.
- UI tests for critical flows.
- Security-related validation tests.

The application is not considered complete merely because it compiles or displays a dashboard.

Verify these critical end-to-end workflows:

TEST A — OWNER LOGIN

An authorized owner can sign in. An unauthorized user cannot obtain owner permissions merely by registering or modifying the client.

TEST B — PROJECT REGISTRATION

The owner adds a project, refreshes the app, and sees the saved project retrieved from the backend.

TEST C — CONTENT UPDATE

The owner edits a supported field. The backend confirms the write. The website reads the updated value. Failure is reported accurately.

TEST D — CHANGE REVIEW

A code change creates a reviewable proposal. The owner can inspect the diff and validation results.

TEST E — PREVIEW AND DEPLOYMENT

